	"nodes":[
		{"id":"0d548af96ee7c4b4","x":-473,"y":-352,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"[[Session Canvases.base]]\n#Session_Canvas"},
		{"id":"62316ff62122fa05","x":-460,"y":-140,"width":425,"height":210,"type":"text","text":"Within Storm Crest there are some rations that Solaris can take. Also what is in Stu's old home.\n\nFrom Storm Crest it is a 3 day walk in the snow to the Bio Labs. During which a series of events can take place, refer to Armount notes."},
		{"id":"443a3492a7bec89e","x":-460,"y":140,"width":925,"height":410,"type":"text","text":"Within the Bio Labs:\n\nAt the end of the walk way are dozens of wounded goliaths malnourished and broken. Nearly all of them unconscious and barely clinging to life. One recognises Stu, Blandin Thendas Husband.\n\n\"That lightening mark. Stu you're sister has told me so much, my name is Blandin I am her husband. We need your help please Thenda, she's alone at the bottom layer of the Bio Labs. All of our men are either dead or not suit to fight, I am all that can stand, we have tried to go down for her every day for a week and lost many each time we attempted it. Please I don't know what to do, I can't save my wife, I'm a disgrace of a husband, it should be me down there not her.\" \n\nYou can see bite marks and claw marks all over his body, bleeding wounds that are still open and rotted with black ichor pouring from them. \n\n\"Each layer of this place is even worse than the last and at the bottom where you're sister is stuck the most horrifying thing I have ever seen lives. Not even a Beholder holds a candle to this thing. Whatever it is there is no way it is a creation of a God, only men would make something so sinister.\"\n"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}